& [RegistrySolution] retains complete authority visibly
  + registry owns ordered records under one digest and generation
  + each record owns exact typed context plus exactly one checkpoint or terminal outcome under its own digest
  + READ returns the exact compact record JSON rather than hiding process state behind a summary

& [HandleSolution] is compact and stale-safe
  + handle binds registry session sequence record state and checkpoint or outcome identities
  + mutations require complete registry digest session sequence and record digest
  + successful OPEN or ADVANCE increments registry generation and session sequence

& [ExecutionSolution] preserves the stateless reference
  + OPEN strictly parses context JSON and delegates to core BEGIN
  + ADVANCE delegates to core ADVANCE and stores its exact checkpoint or outcome
  + quota-eight OPEN plus two ADVANCE calls reaches the byte-equal stateless terminal outcome

& [McpSolution] is one small volatile control surface
  + continue_procedure_session supports OPEN ADVANCE INSPECT and READ
  + context and record cross the schema boundary as bounded JSON strings while internal values remain typed
  + a process-local mutex admits exactly one of two equal-head writers
  + tool metadata measures 4951 bytes and ordinary quota-eight ADVANCE arguments measure 367 bytes

